Subject: [PATCH] mf: initialize SAR marker linkage before copying its context

stream_place_marker() allocates a zeroed queued_object, then copies a caller's
optional context before inserting the object into the renderer queue. If
PropVariantCopy fails, release_pending_object() calls list_remove() on the
still-NULL links and crashes instead of returning the copy error.

Initialize the entry as an empty self-linked list before that fallible copy.
The existing cleanup can then unlink it safely; successful insertion and
marker delivery remain unchanged. This is independent of the end-marker
demand reset in 0043. Media Session's normal NULL-context EOF markers do not
exercise this allocation/copy-error path.

The extracted actual-source regression injects a copy failure and observes
SIGSEGV with both P6 and 0043 alone, then the original error return with this
patch. No claim is made that this caused the co-test seek freeze.
---
diff --git a/dlls/mf/sar.c b/dlls/mf/sar.c
--- a/dlls/mf/sar.c
+++ b/dlls/mf/sar.c
@@ -1702,6 +1702,7 @@ static HRESULT stream_place_marker(struct audio_renderer *renderer, MFSTREAMSINK_MARKER_TYPE marker_type,
     if (!(marker = calloc(1, sizeof(*marker))))
         return E_OUTOFMEMORY;
 
+    list_init(&marker->entry);
     marker->type = OBJECT_TYPE_MARKER;
     marker->u.marker.type = marker_type;
     PropVariantInit(&marker->u.marker.context);
